  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Potassium permanganate decomposes when heated, the oxidation state of manganese changes as the oxidation state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math> decomposes to potassium manganate which oxidation state is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math> and manganese dioxide its oxidation state is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p>It is a redox reaction in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math> which undergo both oxidation and reduction such type of reaction is known as a disproportionation reaction.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mover><mo>→</mo><mrow><mn>513</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p>"
  }
